    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d152-a3">

                <pb facs="0331" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1877/pg283"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 91.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pierrepont to Lord Tenterden.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-12-20"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 20,
                        1876</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Lord Tenterden</hi>: As it is very desirable
                    to start Brent on his way at the earliest practicable moment, I inclose you a
                    note which I have written to Lord Derby, and hoping that you may facilitate the
                    matter so that there shall be no delay after Lord Derby arrives at the foreign
                    office, I leave the note unsealed, thinking that there may be some formal
                    matters requiring attention with which I am not familiar, but which you
                    understand.</p>
                <p>Very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed>EDWARDS PIERREPONT.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
